'''Yvyra'ara''' ({{Literal translation|forest of the sky}}) is a city that serves as the [[Cites in Balisca|administrative and cultural center]] of the indigenous [[Pindorama]] [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|nation]], the northernmost [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Balisca]]. As of 31 December 2024, the city had an estimated [[W:Population|population]] of 317,405 and a [[W:Population density|population density]] of 6,100 people per km<sup>2</sup> (16,000 persons per sq. mi.). The total area is {{cvt|68.6|km2}}. 

Yvyra'ara is located on the [[Altiplano (Pindorama)|Altiplano]] of [[Pindorama#Geography|Pindorama Island]], the largest of the community. The modern city was officially founded on 6 November 1811. Before that, Yvyra'ara had been for centuries one of the most important and populous sites in Pindorama. 

